WEBVTT

00:02.402 --> 00:03.869
Legend has it that...

00:05.038 --> 00:07.598
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons.

00:08.174 --> 00:13.510
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.981 --> 00:20.146
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.266 --> 00:40.695
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.974 --> 00:46.810
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.348 --> 00:54.253
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.922 --> 00:59.688
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.793 --> 01:02.990
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.766 --> 01:13.831
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:14.007 --> 01:19.843
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.714 --> 01:27.984
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:28.154 --> 01:36.562
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.263 --> 01:38.924
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.675 --> 01:52.111
<i>Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

02:10.864 --> 02:15.460
<i>Ippongi Sekimon</i>

02:41.094 --> 02:42.322
W-What the hell?

02:50.637 --> 02:52.730
It's the Bakufu forces!

03:10.523 --> 03:11.990
The demon has appeared.

03:13.660 --> 03:18.359
<i>The Demon and the Shura</i>

03:21.835 --> 03:24.201
Follow the Vice Commander!

03:34.280 --> 03:35.713
We're up against a small force.

03:35.815 --> 03:37.942
Take out that man on the horse!

03:46.826 --> 03:47.918
Like hell you'll hit me!

03:48.528 --> 03:50.519
What's that man thinking?

03:50.663 --> 03:52.631
He's not going to try to
break through alone, is he?

04:13.086 --> 04:15.145
The barrier at Ippongi
has been breached!

04:15.388 --> 04:16.184
What?

04:16.489 --> 04:18.354
What's the size of the enemy force?

04:18.524 --> 04:20.253
Actually, sir, you see...

04:20.393 --> 04:22.122
It was breached by just one man...

04:22.328 --> 04:23.989
What the hell?

04:24.230 --> 04:25.288
Surely it can't be...

04:25.798 --> 04:26.787
He's coming!

04:28.701 --> 04:30.328
Riflemen! Engage!

04:51.557 --> 04:53.081
That kimono coat...

04:53.259 --> 04:54.692
Those dandara stripes...

04:55.495 --> 04:56.655
The Shinsengumi!

04:57.030 --> 04:58.122
Shinsengumi...

04:58.231 --> 04:59.357
Shinsengumi...

05:04.604 --> 05:08.005
Looks like I've reached
the banks of the River Styx.

05:08.441 --> 05:12.172
Kondo, Soushi, I'll be with you soon!

05:16.549 --> 05:17.447
Go!

05:17.550 --> 05:18.539
Go!

05:41.841 --> 05:42.933
So I got here in time.

05:44.477 --> 05:45.409
Yes.

05:45.878 --> 05:47.869
Who the hell is that man?

05:48.014 --> 05:49.845
He's not one of our men.

05:50.283 --> 05:52.376
But look how frightened the horse is!

05:53.052 --> 05:55.646
Wait, am I just as frightened myself?

05:55.888 --> 05:58.356
My voice is gone!

05:59.192 --> 06:02.787
I have a message from
Okita, just before he died...

06:03.162 --> 06:04.220
I see.

06:07.633 --> 06:12.832
"Soushi died a happy man."
And he said to take care of you.

06:13.740 --> 06:15.970
Take care of me, huh?

06:16.676 --> 06:18.371
Goddamn him!

06:18.544 --> 06:20.171
A meddler until the moment he died!

06:21.481 --> 06:23.210
How many men did you kill?

06:23.383 --> 06:26.978
That sword is a mess,
all nicked and bloody!

06:28.721 --> 06:30.245
You're right.

06:30.456 --> 06:33.948
So? How do you plan
to "take care of me"?

06:34.394 --> 06:36.919
You can't kill me with a sword
like that, that's all I'm saying.

06:37.530 --> 06:39.088
This is Okita's sword.

06:42.101 --> 06:45.036
Okita didn't die of
tuberculosis, I killed him.

06:46.239 --> 06:48.002
He was able to fight, then, was he?

06:48.741 --> 06:50.470
He was a genius, that kid...

06:52.011 --> 06:53.171
I see.

06:53.513 --> 06:57.847
Soushi fought, and then died, eh?

06:58.017 --> 07:00.679
But I'm not going to thank you, Mutsu!

07:01.587 --> 07:03.578
Now you've given me a reason...

07:03.723 --> 07:05.918
I'll fight to avenge Soushi's death!

07:08.361 --> 07:11.125
Besides, my goal for
today was to reach the...

07:11.297 --> 07:12.924
...Staff Headquarters
of the Imperial forces...

07:13.533 --> 07:14.727
Surely not...

07:14.834 --> 07:16.699
Who in their right
mind would even think...

07:17.303 --> 07:20.898
Doesn't he know how many soldiers
there are beyond this point?

07:21.474 --> 07:24.238
Didn't I tell you the first time we met?

07:24.444 --> 07:30.178
"In the future, if I ever find you standing
in my way, then I'll kill you myself!"

07:31.818 --> 07:33.445
Sure I remember!

07:43.296 --> 07:46.390
Why is it that men are
always wanting to fight?

07:46.632 --> 07:47.758
Why?

07:56.409 --> 07:58.934
It looks like I'll get there in time.

08:00.012 --> 08:02.503
It won't be long before
the demon rushes in.

08:05.451 --> 08:07.544
I have to fulfill the
promise I made to Okita.

08:07.987 --> 08:09.511
Give me that sword.

08:09.789 --> 08:11.916
You weren't able to kill me.

08:12.258 --> 08:14.488
So I'm going to do you a favor
and give it to someone who can.

08:16.229 --> 08:20.290
This isn't really a swap, but,
I want you to hold onto this.

08:22.101 --> 08:23.227
What is it?

08:23.469 --> 08:26.802
If for some reason I don't
make it back here alive...

08:27.073 --> 08:29.132
...then take it to my younger brother.

08:29.275 --> 08:30.970
I told you where I come from...

08:31.110 --> 08:33.943
...when we were recovering
from our injuries, didn't I?

08:34.080 --> 08:35.638
I'm pretty sure he's still there.

08:35.748 --> 08:37.181
I guess he must be about fifteen now...

08:38.050 --> 08:40.109
My brother's an eccentric kid...

08:40.286 --> 08:41.878
...but if I die...

08:42.088 --> 08:45.615
...tell him that I said, "You've
got to carry on the Mutsu name now."

08:45.725 --> 08:47.659
If you give him that he'll understand.

08:48.728 --> 08:50.628
You don't think... You're going to lose?

08:51.264 --> 08:52.663
Of course not!

08:52.865 --> 08:55.095
I'm a Mutsu, remember?
There's no way I could lose.

08:56.035 --> 09:00.062
The thing is, Hijikata is
a demon, who loves to fight.

09:00.306 --> 09:04.140
No other man has killed
as much as Hijikata has...

09:04.277 --> 09:06.768
...not since Musashi
Miyamoto himself, I'm sure!

09:07.046 --> 09:08.411
There have been scores of men...

09:08.548 --> 09:11.016
...known as Masters during
the 300 years of Tokugawa rule...

09:11.117 --> 09:14.917
No matter how skilled you may be
with a shinai, it doesn't mean that...

09:15.054 --> 09:16.681
...you're skilled enough to kill.

09:18.991 --> 09:22.518
Skill-wise, Okita is superior.
Because he was a genius.

09:22.628 --> 09:25.426
However, Hijikata's the one to fear.

09:25.665 --> 09:28.327
I fear him more than
anyone else I've met.

09:28.501 --> 09:33.268
He's probably the first demon
I'll be going to meet face to face...

09:33.539 --> 09:36.030
But that's precisely the
reason why I won't lose.

09:36.375 --> 09:38.570
But I can't say I'll win, either.

09:38.778 --> 09:40.040
That's all there is to it.

09:41.147 --> 09:41.772
Wait!

09:42.281 --> 09:43.714
You better go hide.

09:43.916 --> 09:46.942
This is a battlefield.
It's no place for a woman.

09:49.488 --> 09:53.254
Now that I think of it, you still
haven't told me your name, have you?

09:53.693 --> 09:56.218
R-Ran, that's my name.

09:56.596 --> 09:57.654
It's a good name.

09:57.763 --> 10:00.630
You're a real beauty, and you'll
be able to find a good husband.

10:01.467 --> 10:04.664
I already know one woman
whose heart is in the grave...

10:04.770 --> 10:06.328
...and I don't need to know any more.

10:06.472 --> 10:08.406
When everything's settled,
find yourself a husband.

10:09.108 --> 10:13.135
As if anyone would marry
the daughter of a foreigner!

10:13.646 --> 10:15.614
Oh, is that right?

10:15.748 --> 10:17.238
So that's your story?

10:17.450 --> 10:19.077
I never had a clue...

10:19.318 --> 10:20.751
Really, now!

10:20.953 --> 10:23.786
With this red hair of mine,
and these light brown eyes?

10:25.091 --> 10:26.649
You're beautiful, you know.

10:28.027 --> 10:31.224
All this time, that's the
only way I ever saw you.

10:32.198 --> 10:36.259
And I'm sure there are plenty of
other morons like me in the world!

11:02.928 --> 11:04.793
This is it, this is it!

11:05.131 --> 11:08.965
I'm trembling, dammit! More
than I ever have in any battle!

11:09.168 --> 11:11.568
He's pitched slightly
forward and to the right...

11:11.737 --> 11:15.434
It's similar to Okita's stance but
the mindset is entirely different!

11:15.708 --> 11:19.667
This man is made of murderous
intent, and he's insane...

11:44.403 --> 11:45.563
So quick!

11:46.038 --> 11:47.972
I can just barely tell when
he's going to strike, and still...

12:12.531 --> 12:14.556
Can't dodge!

12:15.568 --> 12:16.262
He blocked it!

12:23.509 --> 12:24.999
He's going to jump off me?

13:12.691 --> 13:15.592
You've got to be insane, Hijikata.

13:15.828 --> 13:19.423
After blocking one of my blows,
you came after me with a thrust!

13:19.632 --> 13:21.463
I nearly got myself skewered.

13:21.934 --> 13:24.334
You're the one who's insane.

13:24.570 --> 13:28.404
Okita might've been able to dodge
that blow, but... what the hell was that?

13:28.541 --> 13:31.567
You even managed to elbow
me as a "parting gift"!

13:33.212 --> 13:35.180
This is a lot of fun, isn't it?

13:37.883 --> 13:40.351
Did Soushi use his thrust on you?

13:41.320 --> 13:42.252
Yes.

13:45.257 --> 13:46.724
Is that so!

14:13.719 --> 14:15.812
It's the same as when
he fought Lord Okita...

14:15.988 --> 14:20.186
...no, the difference is that when he
went for the neck after those thrusts...

14:25.898 --> 14:27.525
Thrusting with one hand...

14:27.666 --> 14:30.897
...while blocking my kick to the
chest by drawing a wakizashi...

14:32.671 --> 14:36.835
Since when does the Tennen Rishin
Style use the Two-Sword Technique?

14:37.109 --> 14:39.509
My style is
no-holds-barred...

14:39.645 --> 14:42.307
My instructors were always scolding
me for straying from the basics.

14:46.652 --> 14:48.745
You're a demon, huh, Hijikata?

14:49.555 --> 14:51.284
You're probably right.

15:21.287 --> 15:22.584
I slashed him!

15:23.055 --> 15:24.317
No, I just nicked his skin.

15:28.193 --> 15:31.253
It's no good, I won't be able to swing
upwards with my sword, it's too heavy...

15:41.106 --> 15:44.769
The bastard, he just went
ahead and used his injured foot!

15:57.156 --> 16:00.785
Not only that, but he let me
slash his skin, for god's sake.

16:00.926 --> 16:02.587
My arm's broken.

16:03.329 --> 16:07.197
At any rate, you
bastard, if I'm a demon...

16:09.034 --> 16:11.161
...then you're a Shura!

16:16.609 --> 16:20.477
I can't stop trembling, because
I'm enjoying this so much!

16:21.046 --> 16:23.810
Why don't you join me in hell?

16:39.965 --> 16:42.092
You're losing some control, Mutsu.

17:14.066 --> 17:17.035
Just as I thought, you're not human!

17:17.136 --> 17:19.661
No human would step in like that
to take a full blow from a sword!

17:20.806 --> 17:24.139
Just the hand guard, maybe,
but I did slash you a bit.

17:25.210 --> 17:27.610
Not only that, but
this technique of yours...

17:31.617 --> 17:33.346
Incredible!

17:45.664 --> 17:49.259
Thanks to you, I have no more regrets...

17:53.405 --> 17:56.738
I'm sure no other man has ever slogged
through battle after battle the way I did.

17:56.875 --> 17:59.708
I finally battled myself out...

18:05.050 --> 18:07.075
Now, then, I should be off...

18:07.286 --> 18:10.278
The Gates of Hell are open!

18:17.730 --> 18:20.130
Deputy Commander of the
Shinsengumi...

18:20.232 --> 18:23.463
...Toshizo Hijikata, is on his way!

19:04.977 --> 19:09.277
I had a lot of good
times, Kondo, Soushi...

19:10.048 --> 19:12.278
I have so many stories for you...

19:12.751 --> 19:14.218
Just wait for me!

19:20.726 --> 19:25.459
<i>May 21, 1869 Deputy Commander of</i>
<i>the Shinsengumi Toshizo Hijikata...</i>

19:25.564 --> 19:30.297
<i>... after breaking through the Ippongi</i>
<i>barrier in Hakodate, was killed in action.</i>

19:30.402 --> 19:32.962
<i>He was 35 years old at the time.</i>

19:36.642 --> 19:39.042
There are many legends
and alternative theories...

19:39.144 --> 19:42.204
...regarding the circumstances
of Toshizo Hijikata's death.

19:42.347 --> 19:45.714
The reason may be
because his final battle...

19:45.851 --> 19:50.879
...and the way he died, seemed
altogether too surreal...

19:51.690 --> 19:54.853
Six days after the death of Hijikata...

19:55.160 --> 19:58.493
...Takeaki Enomoto and
his men surrendered...

19:58.764 --> 20:03.895
...bringing the Bakumatsu
Boshin War to an end.

20:25.324 --> 20:26.256
Please wait!

20:27.593 --> 20:31.393
Just put that sword in
my belt, and then go.

20:32.564 --> 20:34.930
But, what about you?

20:36.435 --> 20:38.232
I'm a Mutsu after all.

20:39.004 --> 20:41.199
I couldn't forsake my name.

20:42.274 --> 20:43.206
Go!

20:43.375 --> 20:45.104
And find someone who'll make you
happy!

20:45.244 --> 20:46.336
No, I won't!

20:46.778 --> 20:48.177
I won't let you get away!

20:48.680 --> 20:52.707
I'll follow you, until the day you die...

20:53.785 --> 20:56.652
Until that day comes,
I won't let you escape!

20:57.489 --> 21:02.586
There are no other
morons except for you!

21:04.062 --> 21:08.590
And besides, you still
haven't told me your name!

21:10.969 --> 21:12.698
My name is...

21:31.523 --> 21:37.428
<i>The way ahead is full of twists and</i>
<i>turns, I don't know which way to go.</i>

21:38.964 --> 21:44.834
<i>It feels like I'm gonna get left</i>
<i>behind, so I'm really on edge.</i>

21:46.605 --> 21:50.268
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

21:50.375 --> 21:53.572
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

21:57.115 --> 22:04.180
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

22:04.523 --> 22:10.189
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

22:11.063 --> 22:18.333
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

22:18.737 --> 22:27.145
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

22:27.779 --> 22:29.440
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

22:40.225 --> 22:47.597
<i>Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

22:47.699 --> 22:50.668
<i>The End</i>

23:01.346 --> 23:13.383
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

23:13.658 --> 23:23.397
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

23:23.535 --> 23:32.534
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

23:32.677 --> 23:43.349
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

23:44.389 --> 23:50.521
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

23:50.896 --> 23:53.922
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

23:54.766 --> 24:01.035
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

24:01.339 --> 24:06.834
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>
